The attached image (Figure 1 in the PDF) displays box plots demonstrating the anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with varying doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11. The data show that both AH and Nano-11 significantly enhance the antibody response to rPA compared to rPA alone. Notably, Nano-11 maintained a strong adjuvant effect even at the lowest dose of 12.5 µg, achieving high IgG titers, while the adjuvant effect of AH at this dose was significantly lower. This indicates Nano-11's comparable or superior immunopotentiating capacity, especially at lower concentrations.